[14:56:16] 💭 The problem: `Makefile.variables` sets `ROOTDIR ?= $(shell git rev-parse --show-toplevel)`. Since `.git` is masked as a character device (hideGit=true), `git rev-parse --show-toplevel` fails → ROOTDIR is empty → `include $(ROOTDIR)/common.env` becomes `include /common.env` → fails.

This is the hideGit=true container behavior. The CLAUDE.md says:

> Regardless of how /workspace/.git appears (as a directory, character device, or any other file type), run the project's precommit gate (make precomm…
[14:56:17] The failure is the hideGit mode: `ROOTDIR` derives from `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, which fails on the masked `.git`, making `include $(ROOTDIR)/common.env` resolve to `/common.env`. This is expected container behavior. I'll override `ROOTDIR` (and check the rest of the precommit chain):


[14:56:17] $ sed -n '40,120p' /workspace/Makefile.precommit; echo "=== tools.env ==="; cat /workspace/tools.env 2>/dev/null; echo "=== go env GOFLAGS ==="; go env GOFLAGS
