[14:56:25] 💭 `Makefile.docker` uses git but only inside build/upload targets (not at parse time). `common.env` doesn't reference git/ROOTDIR/BRANCH. So overriding `ROOTDIR=/workspace` should let `make precommit` parse and run.

Note: `make precommit` runs `format` which modifies files (gofmt, goimports-reviser, golines) — that's expected, it's part of the precommit gate. It also runs `go mod tidy` and `rm -rf vendor` in `ensure`. This is the standard precommit chain.

Let me run `make precommit ROOTDIR=/work…
